--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Architecture (matches established sibling W7 pages: FeedbackQueuePage / TripPlannerPage)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- MVVM, no business logic in code-behind. The view binds AlertRulesPageViewModel and
  renders the pure AlertRulesDisplay projection; all branch selection / formatting /
  i18n happen in the headless Model. State changes marshalled onto the UI thread.
- Data port IAlertRulesFeed (web hooks) -> generated C# OpenAPI client (ADR-004):
    useAlertRules        -> get_api_v1_alerts_rules               GET  /alerts/rules
    useBulkEnableRules   -> post_api_v1_alerts_rules_bulk_enable  POST /alerts/rules/bulk/enable  { ids }
    useBulkDisableRules  -> post_api_v1_alerts_rules_bulk_disable POST /alerts/rules/bulk/disable { ids }
    useDeleteAlertRule   -> delete_api_v1_alerts_rules_ruleID     DELETE /alerts/rules/{ruleID}
    useSaveAlertRule     -> put_api_v1_alerts_rules_ruleID        PUT  /alerts/rules/{ruleID}     { name }
  (op ids cross-checked against apps/windows/Generated ApiEndpoints.All — all present.)
- Shared Fluent components reused (no web pixel-cloning, ADR-005/006):
    TsGlassPanel, PageTitle, Subhead, Label, Text, ErrorText, TsSkeleton (loading),
    TsErrorDisplay (error), TsEmptyState (empty + CTA), TsCheckbox (master tri-state +
    per-row), TsEditableText (inline rename), TsBadge (enabled/disabled status),
    TsSeverityBadge (severity chip), TsButton (Open Alert Studio).
    EditConflictBanner shared surface (web EditConflictBanner + useEditLease) over
    StaticEditLeaseSource with resourceLabel = editConflict.resource.alertRules.
    BulkActionsToolbar shared surface (web BulkActionToolbar + useBulkSelection +
    useConfirm) with enable/disable/delete(+confirm) actions and the rule item-noun.
- i18n: every visible literal flows through ILocalizer.GetString("<key>","<English fallback>").
  Per the established W7 contract the page keys resolve through the WinUI resource
  bridge and fall back to the verbatim web English copy (sibling DONE pages add no
  resw rows; the keyed call site IS the resolution path). Headless tests assert every
  key is requested (RecordingLocalizer) and that the fallbacks match the web verbatim.
- Units: this page has no SI-unit fields (rules list); nothing stored/computed non-SI.
- Live data: this page has no live/SSE source (the web page is a TanStack query only),
  so no >2min staleness chrome is applicable (matches the web source).

